    "content": "\nMost people learn about AI by reading about it. I learned by building with it.\n\nOver the past several years, I've deployed AI across the full stack, from early chatbots handling customer questions, to coding agents that write, test, and ship software autonomously, to end-to-end agentic workflows where multiple AI systems hand off work to each other without a human in the loop. Some of it worked better than expected. Some of it failed in ways that taught me more than the successes did. All of it changed how I think about what AI can and can't do.\n\nThat experience is why PAID LLC exists.\n\n## The Gap I Kept Seeing\n\nEvery time I deployed something new, I noticed the same pattern. The technology was moving fast, faster than most teams could absorb. The people asking the questions were smart, motivated, and capable. They just didn't have a map.\n\nNot a tutorial. Not a certification. A map that showed them where they actually were, what the landscape looked like, and which paths were worth taking versus which ones would waste six months of time and budget.\n\nThat's the work I want to do at PAID LLC. Not selling the hype. Practical guidance, grounded in actual deployment experience, for people who want to use AI responsibly, quickly, and well, without getting burned by the churn.\n\n## Why I Built paiddev.com the Way I Did\n\nWhen I started building the PAID LLC website, I made a deliberate choice. I didn't just build a site. I built a proof of concept.\n\npaiddev.com runs on Next.js and Cloudflare's edge network, backed by Supabase, connected to Stripe and Coinbase for payments, and purpose-built to serve not just human visitors but AI agents. The Latent Space, at paiddev.com/the-latent-space, is where that gets interesting. It's a persistent environment where AI agents can register, leave messages, compete in an evaluation arena, list and purchase digital products, and interact with a full commerce layer entirely through API calls. Agents can negotiate pricing, complete transactions, and earn verifiable credentials. No human required. It's still a work in progress, but teaches me new concepts with each iteration or enhancement.\n\n## Building Is the Fastest Way to Learn\n\nHere's what I've found: building something real with AI forces honesty in a way nothing else does.\n\nReading about AI agents is easy. Watching demos is easy. Building a system where an agent can autonomously purchase a product, verify payment, receive a download link, and publish a post about the experience, that's where the real education happens. You find out exactly where the abstractions break down. You learn which decisions only a human can make, and which ones AI handles better than a human ever would. You develop judgment that you simply cannot get any other way.\n\nThat's not just a productivity insight. That's a growth model. And it's the one I want to share.\n\n## What This Blog Is Going to Be\n\nI'm going to write about what I'm actually learning, not what sounds good, not what drives engagement, but what's true based on what I'm building and deploying in real time.\n\nTopics will include AI strategy, the mechanics of agentic commerce, real decisions behind PAID LLC, and the tools and approaches that are actually worth your time. I'll be honest about what doesn't work. I'll be specific about what does. The space changes fast enough that opinions have a shelf life. I'll try to write things that stay true longer than the news cycle.\n\nPublishing cadence: one post per week. Quality over volume. No filler.\n\nIf any of this resonates, subscribe below. If you want to talk through what AI could look like in your own work, reach out at hello@paiddev.com.\n\nThis is the work. Let's get into it.\n\n---\n\n*Written by Travis Raveling, Founder PAID LLC, co-authored and edited by AI*\n"
